# .servicepackupdateignore
# Files and patterns to exclude when updating servicepack framework
# Uses rsync exclude syntax - supports wildcards and paths

# Example: Custom framework modifications
# Makefile
# Dockerfile.dev
# .golangci.yml

# Example: Custom scripts
# scripts/custom_*
# scripts/deploy.sh

# Example: Local configuration files
# *.local
# .env*
# config/local.yml

# User files - never overwritten by framework updates
cmd/init.go
cmd/commands.go

# chatz customizes the linter config (depguard allowlist for chatz's own deps,
# ireturn carve-out for the generated strict handlers, lint-exclusion paths for
# servicepack-owned dirs). Keep it project-owned so framework updates don't wipe
# it -- the framework's baseline .golangci.yml would otherwise overwrite ours.
.golangci.yml

# chatz adds its own make targets to the root Makefile (web-* frontend
# lifecycle, test-integration / test-real / test-e2e, run-showcase, etc.). Keep
# it project-owned so framework updates don't clobber them -- the framework's
# baseline Makefile would otherwise overwrite ours.
Makefile

# chatz's pipeline sets has_codegen: true -- it commits gorm repositories, the
# OpenAPI server/client and the embedded GenUI prompt, so it needs the
# codegen-drift gate the framework leaves off by default. The framework's
# pipeline also publishes its agent skill to ClawHub, which chatz does not have.
.github/workflows/pipeline.yml

# The framework ships the agent skill describing SERVICEPACK. Landing it here
# would tell an agent reading chatz that it is looking at the framework repo.
.agents

# --- Project-owned config the framework also ships ---------------------------
#
# Each of these exists in both repos with different contents, so without an
# entry the framework's version silently replaces chatz's.

# chatz's allowlist covers its own untracked paths (web build output, test
# fixtures, the local .env); the framework's covers the framework's.
.gitleaks.toml

# chatz's docker context excludes the web build tree and node_modules, which
# the framework has no concept of.
.dockerignore

# Chatz owns its Go dependency age-gate implementation. Do not introduce a
# duplicate hyphenated framework script beside the project-owned underscore
# variant used by its custom Make targets.
scripts/check-go-age.sh

# chatz pins its own ecosystems (gomod plus the web app's npm tree); the
# framework only knows about gomod.
.github/dependabot.yml

# chatz's production image is not the framework's: it carries a web build stage
# that compiles the SPA and copies it into the go:embed dir, it targets ./cmd
# explicitly (./cmd/... would also match cmd/repogen), and its ldflags stamp
# chatz's own buildinfo package plus the binary's identity. The framework's
# baseline Dockerfile knows none of that and would overwrite all of it.
Dockerfile

# chatz owns its entire test tree: tests/testinfra (a real Postgres + browser
# harness), tests/api, tests/boot, tests/integration, tests/fakeupstream,
# tests/mcpserver, tests/real. servicepack v1.8.0+ ships its own minimal
# tests/testinfra + tests/integration baseline that would otherwise overwrite
# chatz's (rsync has no --delete, but it does overwrite same-path files). Keep
# the framework out of tests/ entirely.
tests/

# Note: internal/pkg/services/* is always excluded - your services are never touched
